=== 
--- calls
exit: 0
--- stdout
chase — host wrapper

Read-only scraper for the Chase retail relationship: deposit accounts
(checking / savings) and credit-card reads. `download` is a one-shot
login + scrape with 2FA driven from the terminal; `load` builds the SQLite
silver. See DESIGN.md "Source behaviour" for the mapped flows.

Subcommands:
  build               Build the Docker image (`docker build`).
  download [args...]  One-shot login + scrape with 2FA driven from the
                      TERMINAL (no VNC): pre-fills + submits the sign-in
                      form, prompts for the code on stdin (push / SMS /
                      voice), then exports each account's activity (CSV +
                      QFX) and statement PDFs into a UTC-stamped bronze run
                      dir. --lookback bounds the statement pass (the
                      activity export always fetches Chase's full ~24
                      months); --no-documents skips statements; --dry-run
                      walks without exporting.
  vnc-login [args...] Fallback for download when the CLI 2FA can't drive a
                      challenge control: exposes VNC for a by-hand sign-in.
  login [args...]     Folds into download (the session dies with Firefox,
                      §F). `login --check` probes a session read-only
                      (exit 0 alive / 1 dead).
  load [args...]      Ingest bronze into the SQLite silver (accounts,
                      transactions, statements). --force rebuilds from all
                      bronze.
  prune [args...]     Delete non-complete dumps from the bronze tree, and
                      aged entries of the /debug cache (runs host-side).
                      --dry-run prints the plan.
  explore [args...]   Discovery harness: Camoufox over VNC + HAR / network
                      log / click log / trace under /debug. --fresh wipes
                      the profile so the next login forces a full 2FA.
  sh|bash             Open an interactive shell in the container.
  help                Show this message.

Mounted into the container:
  <TMP>/w-chase/home/.secrets  ->  /secrets
  <TMP>/w-chase/xdgdata/wealthdb/chase     ->  /data
  <TMP>/w-chase/xdgcache/wealthdb/startupcache  ->  /cache/startupcache
  <TMP>/w-chase/xdgcache/wealthdb/chase  ->  /cache/collector
  <TMP>/w-chase/xdgcache/wealthdb/debug/chase    ->  /debug

Override mounts via env:
  CHASE_SECRETS_DIR=/path/to/secrets
  CHASE_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data
  CHASE_DEBUG_DIR=/path/to/debug

Credentials:
  CHASE_USERNAME / CHASE_PASSWORD are read from /secrets/chase.env inside
  the container (= $HOME/.secrets/chase.env on the host). chmod 0600.
  `download` drives the 2FA challenge from the terminal; `vnc-login`
  and `explore` leave it to be completed by hand over VNC.
